    {
      "name": "B318",
      "source": "# R108: parimana() - one number, the bytes the program's nirmmita and kosh hold now - moving as\n# allocations happen. A block gives back its nirmmita; a kosh (made inside a block or not) keeps its\n# header and capacity for the program's life: kosh storage is not reclaimed yet.\nmukhya() {\n    likha(\"start \", parimana(), \"\\n\")\n    kosh k[1]\n    kosh_kship(k, 1)\n    likha(\"a kosh of 1 \", parimana(), \"\\n\")\n    kosh_kship(k, 2)\n    kosh_kship(k, 3)\n    likha(\"grown to capacity 4 \", parimana(), \"\\n\")\n    mandapa {\n        vitti b = nirmmita(100)\n        likha(\"a block's nirmmita(100) \", parimana(), \"\\n\")\n        kosh m[8]\n        likha(\"and a kosh of 8 in it \", parimana(), \"\\n\")\n    }\n    likha(\"after the block \", parimana(), \"\\n\")\n}\n",
      "compile": {
        "command": [
